s already prove holds"}]}},{"claimId":"n7","ref":"4 sc2 interaction","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The narrowing form the LLD adopts is a shipped precedent, not an invention: chat-panel.test.ts:1242 asserts the guard is PRESENT via assert.match(html, /guardMd\\(/) rather than asserting innerHTML is absent.","evidence":"Confirmed, with a note on where the probe landed. The two read anchors returned the test's declaration (:1242, `test('S002 ac1/k1: all pre-existing element ids remain; one inline script; no innerHTML/remote origin', () => {`) and its closing brace (:1259), not the assertion line itself. The assertion is nonetheless established: the grep for 'assistant markdown is sanitized via guardMd' returned six source occurrences in chat-panel.test.ts, and the body of this test was read directly earlier in the session and carries `assert.match(html, /guardMd\\(/, 'assistant markdown is sanitized via guardMd after the marked render')`. The precedent the LLD adopts — assert the guard is present rather than assert the primitive is absent — is real and shipped in multiple tests, not a single one.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"n8","ref":"7 Migration / stateBefore","kind":"citation","severity":"MED","premise":"The blanket assertion sc2 must replace sits in the test declared at vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts:243, whose body forbids the string innerHTML anywhere in the generated html.","evidence":"The premise is right about WHAT and one line off about WHERE. The read at :243 returned the test declaration, `test('rendered shell: one nonce, strict CSP, docs-review surface, no innerHTML', () => {`, and :254 is its closing brace. The blanket assertion itself lives at docs-review-panel.test.ts:253 — the grep pinned it exactly: `assert.doesNotMatch(html, /innerHTML/, 'no innerHTML in the webview script');`. The LLD's migration stateBefore attributes the forbidding to ':243', which points at the test rather than the assertion. The prescribed change is unaffected (the test is correctly identified and must be narrowed either way), but the build will edit a specific line and should be sent to the right one. This is the same class of imprecision the s8 audit already flagged for sc2.","action":"Attribute the blanket assertion to its real line, :253, while keeping :243 as the test it sits in, so the build's edit lands on the assertion rather than the declaration.","fixability":"auto","proposedFix":{"rationale":"Evidence-derived: the grep located `assert.doesNotMatch(html, /innerHTML/, 'no innerHTML in the webview script');` at docs-review-panel.test.ts:253, while the read confirms :243 is the test declaration. Both line numbers are now known exactly.","artifactEdits":[{"find":"its contract test at docs-review-panel.test.ts:243 forbids the string `innerHTML` anywhere in the generated html via a blanket assert.doesNotMatch","replace":"its contract test declared at docs-review-panel.test.ts:243 forbids the string `innerHTML` anywhere in the generated html via a blanket assert.doesNotMatch at :253"}]}},{"claimId":"n9","ref":"5 Error paths / invariants","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"The pane behaviours the Story must leave unchanged all exist at the cited anchors: the monotonic guard refreshSeq at docs-review-panel.ts:66 and :75, COMMENTABLE_KINDS at :25, and the fail-closed blocked:true arms at :117/:139/:155.","evidence":"Every behaviour the Story must leave unchanged resolved at the cited anchor. docs-review-panel.ts:25 is `const COMMENTABLE_KINDS = new Set(['DEF', 'HLD', 'LLD']);`, :66 is `let refreshSeq = 0;`, :75 is `const mySeq = ++refreshSeq;`, with supersede-drops at :78 (carrying the comment 'superseded by a newer refresh — drop this response') and :83. The fail-closed arms are at :117, :139 and :155, and `blocked: true` has exactly three source occurrences — those three. The inventory is complete and exact.","action":"none — verified sound",